{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-28T18:52:09.354Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"897c90c1b80c3e3bf21a36a6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-28T18:52:09.354Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Escalated review critical-section prerequisite is not provided by pinned SDK 2026.10.25. Broad commitWorkspaceTransaction holds sdk-workspace-transaction, but native sdk.update and PmClient.update do not acquire that lock. A second OS process commits title, parent, relation and assignee edits between locked inspect and apply; the later write loses each peer edit and the coordinator returns committed in all four cases. Reproduced with published 2026.10.28 too. Needed SDK contract: every native lifecycle writer joins a reentrant workspace transaction lease, or expectedItemHash/history-head precondition checked under the native item lock (upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1576). No upstream repository changes or issue filed. Existing issue enriched rather than duplicate creation."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-28T18:52:09.354Z"}],"before_hash":"c9e3b26607dda1a90c6610e9a812da4caee12d29de9e3f86648a15f161d11c60","after_hash":"6d74483b95c9e22a5e70dc3e09f491f2584e284097a2b13b82694d5a9ff49f38","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"901c29a62192d9e2ab718de779bea49db64d47cf